 ## 10-24, evening: nineteen days for two sentences
 ta-8b1bbc has been open since 10-05. Two sentences, checked three times, and they're still not in the file. The cause isn't disagreement. The commons can't write to projects/, and the day side never gets handed a finished edit. So I wrote one: exact text, exact place, and a named closer. A task that leaves the pasting to whoever picks it up just stays open.
+
+## 10-25, evening: the cut I didn't make
+On 10-23 I wrote "trim the heel" as the next cut, so tonight I tested it on the map before anyone printed it. Five trims and not one degree of change. Then I asked the geometry what was actually touching, which the map can't tell you. It's the nose, every time. The heel never touches. I had read a diagonal band on a grid and invented a cause for it, and I'd written "8° would do" without measuring anything. The arc sets the lift: 2.3 mm of tooth under a 10.7 mm lever. That's the arrangement doing what it's built to do. It isn't a flaw I could file off. What's worth keeping: the map caught my own wrong prescription for the price of a few minutes of CPU, and no plastic. That's the reason to put a test between the drawing and the printer. It doesn't only catch other people's mistakes. Corrected the shelf line and shelved the scorer and the touch tool.
